From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:17:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: tv: Clean up the encoder when bind defers

When no CRTC is found for the TV encoder, sun4i_tv_bind() returns
-EPROBE_DEFER through err_disable_clk. The encoder is initialised by
then and is left on the mode_config list. struct sun4i_tv is allocated
with devm_kzalloc() in bind, so it is freed when the component framework
releases the devres group of the failed bind, and the next walk of the
encoder list, in drm_mode_config_cleanup(), touches freed memory.

Go through err_cleanup_encoder instead, as the connector error path
already does, so the encoder is removed from the list before the
memory goes.

Not covered: the other error paths of bind, which already unwind in the
right order.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: not tested; the TV encoder is not on the A733
display path.

Fixes: 78428d672c2e ("drm/sun4i: tv: Switch to drm_of_find_possible_crtcs")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tv.c
index ce22f1662c0c..c00b12e241c0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tv.c
@@ -489,7 +489,7 @@ static int sun4i_tv_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 								dev->of_node);
 	if (!tv->encoder.possible_crtcs) {
 		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
-		goto err_disable_clk;
+		goto err_cleanup_encoder;
 	}
 
 	drm_connector_helper_add(&tv->connector,
